# podbox run exit 0
--- stdout
SEEN=yes
CLEARED=yes
--- stderr, without the completion layer
podbox 0.1.0: mode=chroot (namespaces: none; mounts: none; devices: shimmed;
ownership: virtualized+sidecar; network: host-shared; pids: host-shared)
probes: clone(NEWNS)=EPERM mount=EPERM fsmount=skip(EPERM) move_mount=skip(EPERM)
        clone(NEWUTS)=EPERM sethostname=skip(EPERM) chroot=ok ptrace=ok
this mode does NOT provide: process, network, IPC or mount isolation
⚠ this machine would permit `supervise`; podbox's entry sequence is `chroot` and creates no namespace and mounts nothing
podbox: interpose: /.podbox/interpose.so (glibc object) is preloaded for this payload. ⛔ podbox WROTE that file into the image's own rootfs and the payload can see it
